    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "642fc759_c3fde616",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1125984
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T00:14:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suppose it does make more sense to reuse this host event. But then, how do we avoid wakes from other \"PD MCU\" events such as simply plugging in a charger or removing a charger? Or do we let dark resume handle it?",
      "parentUuid": "7a338a39_19d3cd7d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "c249cf48cad12b39f4a2ab004d32ec7caab3f982",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a5607abd_41395529",
        "filename": "include/ec_commands.h",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 600,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003000
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-06-20T00:34:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, that is an interesting point. We do not currently have AC insert/remove as wake events. Ravi -- is this something that can be detected by powerd? Probably powerd will have to worry about individual PD events here?",
      "parentUuid": "642fc759_c3fde616",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 600,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 600,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "c249cf48cad12b39f4a2ab004d32ec7caab3f982",
